    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 28 with a lineup anchored by **Colt Keith**, who earns today\u2019s top efficiency score at 69.64. Facing Grayson Rodriguez and his inflated 4.95 xERA, **Colt Keith** benefits from the prime leadoff spot and a significant platoon advantage, making him our most reliable source of R and HR upside. **Kazuma Okamoto** (62.30) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.08) also provide strong value. Despite the daunting task of facing Paul Skenes, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a vital start; his elite sprint speed is non-negotiable for our SB-starved roster, and the projected wind-out conditions at the stadium provide a marginal boost to his power profile. **Yordan Alvarez** rounds out our high-floor tier (60.07), as his elite .422 xwOBA remains the most reliable engine in our offense regardless of the matchup against Nathan Eovaldi.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, particularly regarding our middle infield. While **Chase Meidroth** (56.92) grades out as a solid start against Simeon Woods Richardson, **Caleb Durbin** sits on the razor's edge with a 41.87 score. His placement at the bottom of the order against a Cy Young-caliber arm in Chris Sale significantly compresses his ceiling, keeping him in the lineup only due to the scarcity of alternatives. Among our reserves, **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Christian Yelich** are unavailable due to scheduled off-days, effectively simplifying our roster construction today. Should **Dillon Dingler** struggle early against Rodriguez, we will look to pivot to the high-contact approach of **Lars Nootbaar** or **Josh Smith** in upcoming sets, provided their schedule allows. Owners should monitor the weather in Pittsburgh, as any late-breaking precipitation could negatively impact the scoring potential for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**.",
